pmdomain: gpcv2 still handshakes the GPUMIX signals from the GPU domain's
parent_bits, after the chain merged those macros away.

Adapted from
  https://cdn.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/v6.x/incr/patch-6.12.69-70.xz

That level merged IMX8MM_GPUMIX_HSK_PWRDN{REQN,ACKN} into the GENMASK-ed
IMX8MM_GPU_HSK_PWRDN* macros and dropped the handshake from the GPUMIX parent
entry -- the macro hunks applied to this tree, the entry hunk did not, so the
entry still names macros that no longer exist. The two lines go; the parent
keeps its pxx/map/pgc.

--- a/drivers/pmdomain/imx/gpcv2.c
+++ b/drivers/pmdomain/imx/gpcv2.c
@@ -930,8 +930,6 @@
 		.parent_bits = {
 			.pxx = IMX8MM_GPUMIX_SW_Pxx_REQ,
 			.map = IMX8MM_GPUMIX_A53_DOMAIN,
-			.hskreq = IMX8MM_GPUMIX_HSK_PWRDNREQN,
-			.hskack = IMX8MM_GPUMIX_HSK_PWRDNACKN,
 			.pgc = BIT(IMX8MM_PGC_GPUMIX),
 		},
 
